{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177952-the-supernatural-as-hunters","id":177952,"title":"The Supernatural as Hunters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-23T09:03:12-07:00","id":177952,"title":"The Supernatural as Hunters?","content":"Hi everyone!<br /> <br /> I haven't played much in quite awhile. Last time I really played was as a power hungry Malkovian who was looking to infiltrate the Lucifuge (the book even slightly hinted at the leader being a vampire). <br /> <br /> My question is, has anyone run a game where the conspiracies allowed various members of the supernatural to join their ranks? Maybe one cell who simply wants to keep the peace in a city, aligns themselves with the supernatural as a form of peace treaty. To help ease each others minds, they have to basically have a &quot;foreign exchange student&quot; system in place. A vampire or werewolf would be allowed in the cell, while a member or two from the cell joins the clan and/or pack. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T09:09:06-07:00","id":177984,"title":"","content":"Never so much allowed in, because secrets are secrets, but I've seen and done alliances.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, it's often better for supernaturals to work in their respective groups(demons with demons, changelings with changelings, etc.) on hunting things because their fellows have a better understanding of their members issues and capacity to deal with them than a hunter cell/compact/conspiracy would be. The same applies to hunters-Prometheans might know how to sew up bodies and make them run on improvised parts, but it'd be dangerous for them to try and work on someone with Thaumaturgy Endowments going whack, as an example.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, as Mortal Remains did a great job of pointing out, common enemies are easy to find, and hunter cells and coteries/packs/cabals/throngs/motleys/krewes/henets/rings who actually take time to talk might easy start sharing responsibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-23-2014, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T09:34:34-07:00","id":178012,"title":"","content":"It depends on the compact/conspiracy/cell and which type of Supernatural. It is mentioned in the Sin-Eater book that it sometimes happens, that a Sin-Eater joins up with Hunter cells temporarily, to solve some ghosts anchor or hunt down somebody/something coursing alot of death and disturbing the ghosts. Meanwhile, Sin-Eaters are not as easy to spot by Hunters as, say, a Vampire or Promethean, so they run less risk when doing so.<br /> A Promethean or Vampire on the other hand, has alittle reason to join up with Hunters and the Hunters might spot the unnatural nature of the being at any moment, and if they do, they'll most likely kill it.<br /> Of course not all Hunters are like this. I could easily see a member of The Acending Ones or the Lucifuge be pretty accepting to a Supernatural being, wishing to join their cell in order to hunt something. Meanwhile, something like Task Force; Valkyrie would never let them join, and the field operatives of the Cheiron Group would probably feign agreement at first, and then butcher the Supernatural at first chance. For parts, of course...<br /> The Aegis Kai Duro might accept the help of some Supernaturals, but Mages. They have good reason to really hate Mages.<br /> <br /> And then you have something like The Promethean Brotherhood, who try to steal Gnosis from Mages. If for some reason, a Mage was willing to help them perfect the ritual by which they steal Gnosis and perhaps even help them point out and hunt down new subjects on which they could attempt this new buffed ritual, they would likely welcome him with open arms and kisses.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I'd say that the chance of anyone welcomming a Vampire or Werewolf, is increadibly slim. They have a pretty bad reputation from the folk lore which everyone are aware of, so many will just think &quot;Oh? Its a Vampire! A blood-feasting demon, whose unholy skin burns in the sun! Kill it with fire!&quot; and &quot;Oh? Its a Werewolf! An insane bloodthirsty monster, whose very presence incurs insanity and whose bite will turn you into a monsters yourself! Kill it with Fire/Silver!&quot;. Mages might be accepted, depending on the Hunters personal view, though many will be mistrustful at first. As for the others, they dont have enough of a folk-loric presence for many Hunters to really know whats what, so for those, it comes down to a case by case, basis.<br /> Except for Promethean. Everyone hates the Promethean.<br /> <br /> Thats how I generally look at it, anyway.<br /> <br /> Cheers ~ Krobeles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T11:06:01-07:00","id":178068,"title":"","content":"Awesome!<br /> <br /> That's pretty much how I was picturing it myself. Although I could see TF:V allying themselves with a lesser evil to take down something worse (ex. an established vampire coterie vs new pack of werewolves. While the vampires are a danger to the populace, they have already been there and wish to have a quite existence, trying to not draw attention to themselves. Where as the new pack might run rampant through the streets if there happens to be a locus at the local library (or something similar)).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:07:52-07:00","id":178121,"title":"","content":"In one of my settings, the Summer Court (Changeling) frequently works with local tier 1 Hunters. They exploit each other and know it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T16:29:24-07:00","id":181366,"title":"","content":"Well, I've now written an entire Conspiracy based on facilitating this.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> But, to make this more than a shameless advertisement, essentially, an angle worth considering is Hunter vs Hunter, and how the supernatural would exploit that. For example, say Network 0 gets tired of being pushed around by say, Task Force: VALKYRIE, and decides to team up with monsters getting tired of them as well to disrupt them. Another would be perhaps other Hunter Cells deciding the Ashwood Abbey has gone way too far recently, and are willing to team up with those related to recent victims to take them down. <br /> <br /> Both of these cases poke further at what it means to be a Hunter by calling into question why they hunt only the supernatural, and whether say, Vampires are automatically immoral. Such moral quandaries will leave many Hunters confused at least, if not worse, but are also ones I'd imagine would come up for an experienced cell sooner or later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T16:54:29-07:00","id":181402,"title":"","content":"An all-supernatural group would be an interesting concept for a Compact. Too bad you'd have to limit it to one supernatural group probably for it not to get too chaotic.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's always that old trope of the supernatural hunter group full of &quot;reformed&quot; supernaturals to be used as agents. (Hellboy etc.)<br /> <br /> Maybe the real VII (VtR) is just that.A highly influental human conspiracy that brainwashes supernatural creatures (maybe indoctrinates Rogues if they can be found early enough, or maybe even tries to &quot;upgrade&quot; loyal human agents to monsterhood).<br /> <br /> But of course, such a thing doesn't work too well if it is universal; crossover cosologies tend to not work too well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T18:21:34-07:00","id":181488,"title":"","content":"I actually had a bit of a weird idea earlier today:<br /> <br /> What if all the Major Templates were just a group of &quot;rogue&quot; Conspiracies? Hunted by other hunters because their members end up descending into Slasher-dom at a much higher rate than the others, and because their Endowments leave them less human.<br /> <br /> Vampires could be the Kindred of Lazarus, whose Endowment, The Hungry Beast, requires them to forcefully take the blood of others (and addicts them to it), but lets them pull of vampiric powers.<br /> <br /> Changelings could be the Hedgerow Kids, a loose knit collection of abductees, madmen, and abuse victims who found the backroads into the Hedge, where they gained their Endowment, Pledge. Thanks to their new friends, <i>no one</i> will ever hurt them again.<br /> <br /> And so on and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T18:23:49-07:00","id":181490,"title":"","content":"@amechra: You may want to look at my write-up for Sin-Eaters as a Hunter conspiracy. It's a few threads down on this forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T18:54:13-07:00","id":181506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177952-the-supernatural-as-hunters?p=178121#post178121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of my settings, the Summer Court (Changeling) frequently works with local tier 1 Hunters. They exploit each other and know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing spring, I'm sure they take a whole new level to the term &quot;Friends with benefits&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T20:23:11-07:00","id":181586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177952-the-supernatural-as-hunters?p=181506#post181506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Knowing spring, I'm sure they take a whole new level to the term &quot;Friends with benefits&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hilariously enough, both I and my entire gaming group loathe Spring, simply because we can't find a way to make them interesting. <i>Arkham</i> has them so powerless as to be nonexistant, and those rare few Spring courtiers are dismissed as selfish children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T20:34:43-07:00","id":181595,"title":"","content":"Eh, they could be bring the benefits of the Ashwood Abbey without their crazy bits in this instance.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a related note, I may have a Compact coming up where anyone can be a member, as long as they're willing to participate in their... well, rather illicit activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:56:57-07:00","id":182065,"title":"","content":"I think this is covered under the term &quot;Cancer Cells&quot;. It's up to the individual cells and the philosophies of their Compacts or Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> A cell of The Union, for example, one of whom's number was captured and Embraced, may accept that member back into their fold, if they are able to keep their appetites limited to the local dairy cows and never kill a human.<br /> <br /> A cell of the Cheiron Group or TF:V may readily accept one of the Awakened or the Urathra to observe their capabilities &quot;in the field&quot;. Little do the members of the cell know, but the higher-ups want to couple that data with a vivisection/autopsy to find out how to give other agents those abilities.<br /> <br /> Network Zero wouldn't give it a second thought to have a friendly Supernatural who'd be willing to show off their abilities left and right. The Mallus Malefecarum wouldn't give it a second thought to burn one at the stake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:36:52-07:00","id":182580,"title":"","content":"Actually according to compacts and conspiracies Cheiron Group has spies among the witches and vampires, even going so far as to bribe them with thaumatech, so one can say they're halfway there anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T00:14:28-07:00","id":182685,"title":"","content":"One could argue that the Lancea Sanctum (Vampire), some Created who follow the Refinements of both Ferrum and Stannum (Promethean), the Court of Summer (Changeling), Sin-Eaters who follow the Gatekeeper or Reaper archetypes (Geist), and Unchained of the Saboteur agenda (Demon) all count as Supernatural 'hunters' of a sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:46:13-07:00","id":182981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177952-the-supernatural-as-hunters?p=182685#post182685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could argue that the Lancea Sanctum (Vampire), some Created who follow the Refinements of both Ferrum and Stannum (Promethean), the Court of Summer (Changeling), Sin-Eaters who follow the Gatekeeper or Reaper archetypes (Geist), and Unchained of the Saboteur agenda (Demon) all count as Supernatural 'hunters' of a sort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To further this up Vampires or specifically Mekhet have a whole entire bloodline based on it The Khabit bloodline","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:38:40-07:00","id":189894,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, a supernatural splat thats all about hunting...no, too silly to imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:40:20-07:00","id":189898,"title":"","content":"Okay, on a more serious note. Idigam Chronicles allows for Hunters to be part of Werewolf Packs. So I think that's one route the Devs are heavily endorsing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:44:03-07:00","id":189901,"title":"","content":"It allows <i>humans</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T10:58:56-07:00","id":190485,"title":"","content":"I'm playing it backwards right now. My mage character was a member of the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood when she was in college. Now she's a GoV Acanthus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T13:05:50-07:00","id":190647,"title":"","content":"Oh, that's just <i>unfair</i> to the MBS.<br /> <br /> BTW, what was it like playing one. I think they're pretty awesome, but have never played one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T13:26:04-07:00","id":190668,"title":"","content":"<